WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 9.4 · Financial Management
Restricted and unrestricted funds

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Know which money is committed to what, from the first grant or gift with conditions.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:27.393
Some money can be used only for a purpose a funder set; other money you can use for anything within your mission. The kind of money decides who can change how it is spent.

4
00:00:27.793 --> 00:00:28.393
Four kinds of money

5
00:00:28.393 --> 00:00:39.722
Restricted: Only for the purpose the funder or donor set; changes need their written agreement. For example: A start-up grant that may only pay for the pilot tutoring programme.

6
00:00:39.722 --> 00:00:48.830
Unrestricted: Your initiative decides how to use it, within its mission. For example: General donations, profit from sales and the founders’ own contributions.

7
00:00:48.830 --> 00:01:00.900
Designated: Unrestricted money the founders set aside for a purpose; they can change that decision themselves. For example: The repair café sets money aside for its first proper set of tools.

8
00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:12.689
Deferred: Money received in advance, earned only when you deliver the work or goods. For example: Parents pay term fees in September for tutoring delivered until December.

9
00:01:13.089 --> 00:01:13.689
Why the kind matters

10
00:01:13.689 --> 00:01:20.474
1. Using restricted money elsewhere, even for weeks, can break the agreement or the law.

11
00:01:20.474 --> 00:01:25.778
2. Flexible money is what covers your core costs and risks.

12
00:01:25.778 --> 00:01:32.081
3. Funders trust initiatives that can show where their money went.

13
00:01:32.481 --> 00:01:33.081
What it feeds into

14
00:01:33.081 --> 00:01:38.756
1. Your funds register: one code per restricted fund, with its balance.

15
00:01:38.756 --> 00:01:44.059
2. Your bookkeeping and funder reports, recording spending against each code.

16
00:01:44.059 --> 00:01:50.363
3. Your cash flow and reserves, which rely on flexible money.

17
00:01:50.763 --> 00:01:51.363
What to avoid

18
00:01:51.363 --> 00:01:56.667
Reading the grant conditions after accepting the money, not before.

19
00:01:56.667 --> 00:02:01.600
Treating pre-orders or advance fees as money already earned.

20
00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:07.904
Relying almost entirely on restricted money, with little flexible income.

21
00:02:08.504 --> 00:02:10.304
You set up your funds register, even with one or two lines.

22
00:02:10.304 --> 00:02:14.304
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

23
00:02:15.804 --> 00:02:18.904
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
